# Tracer: untyped object definition
#
# Before (did not work):
# let x = 1
# Former behavior: ParseError: Expected operator or $prop in fact
#
# Now (verified):
let x = 1
x = 1
# Current behavior: x is defined and the ordinary fact x = 1 is stored.
#
# Boundary: the right side must already be well-defined; `let x = x` is rejected.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -f examples/01_proof_patterns/let_object_definition.lit
# Implementation: src/parse/parse_def_stmt.rs and src/execute/exec_let_obj_stmt.rs
